 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T08:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**No, it is generally not safe to exercise outdoors in Jurong right now.** \n\nSingapore has been affected by a severe haze situation driven by smoke from regional fires, keeping air quality at unhealthy levels. \n\n* **ActiveSG Restrictions:** Due to the poor air quality, national sports agencies like Sport Singapore have temporarily closed outdoor and non-air-conditioned facilities at ActiveSG sport centres (including those in the western region like Jurong West, Jurong East, and Boon Lay).\n* **Health Advisories:** When the PSI and 1-hour PM2.5 concentrations enter elevated or unhealthy ranges, official guidelines recommend that the general public **reduce prolonged or strenuous outdoor physical exertion**. \n\nIf you want to work out, it is best to shift your exercise indoors to air-conditioned spaces and check the real-time National Environment Agency (NEA) updates via the [myENV app](https://www.nea.gov.sg/) before heading out.",
